From a brand new Debian server:

SET UP THE RAILS USER:
* sudo useradd -m -s $(which bash) rails
* touch /home/rails/.ssh/authorized_keys (Then copy in the contents of the root authorized_keys file)
* sudo passwd rails (went with sleepy)
* sudo adduser rails sudo

SET UP RBENV & INSTALL RUBY:
* sudo apt update
* sudo apt install git curl libssl-dev libreadline-dev zlib1g-dev autoconf bison build-essential libyaml-dev libreadline-dev libncurses5-dev libffi-dev libgdbm-dev
* sudo su rails
* curl -fsSL https://github.com/rbenv/rbenv-installer/raw/HEAD/bin/rbenv-installer | bash
* echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.rbenv/bin:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc
* source ~/.bashrc
* type rbenv (to be sure rbenv is set up correctly)
* rbenv install 3.1.3
* rbenv global 3.1.3
* echo "gem: --no-document" > ~/.gemrc
* gem install bundler

INSTALL NECESSARY LIBS:
(as root)
* sudo apt install --no-install-recommends -y libjemalloc2 libvips pkg-config libpq-dev && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists /var/cache/apt/archives

SET UP NODE:
* sudo su rails
* curl -o- https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nvm-sh/nvm/v0.39.3/install.sh | bash
* source ~/.bashrc
* nvm install v22.13.0
* (as root user) ln -s /home/rails/.nvm/versions/node/v22.13.0/bin/node /usr/bin/node

SET UP POSTGRES:
* sudo apt update
* sudo apt install postgresql postgresql-contrib
* sudo -u postgres psql
* (in psql) create database brickcity_production;
* \q (to exit out of psql)

SET UP SERVICES:
* vim /etc/systemd/system/puma_brick_city_depot_production.service
* Paste in the contents of lib/server_files/puma_service
* vim /etc/systemd/system/sidekiq.service
* Paste in the contents of lib/server_files/sidekiq_service
* sudo systemctl enable sidekiq.service
* systemctl daemon-reload

